1
00:00:04,040 --> 00:00:07,158
Because, you're going to be
joining me on my mission.

2
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:13,080
You see, I'm planning to beat your boss
and take back this city for the people.

3
00:00:13,960 --> 00:00:14,790
What?

4
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:18,337
To rid this city of drug dealing
and child abusing mafiosi,

5
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:21,596
I have no other choice but
to become a mafioso myself.

6
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:23,437
What are you trying to say?

7
00:00:23,520 --> 00:00:26,317
Surely your mission doesn't
involve joining our Syndicate?

8
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:27,937
Do you have any idea what you're saying?

9
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:29,397
What something like that would entail?

10
00:00:29,480 --> 00:00:30,660
Isn't it beautiful?

11
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:33,470
Yeah,

12
00:00:33,580 --> 00:00:35,815
it's risky, but to take back the city,

13
00:00:35,940 --> 00:00:40,234
I have to join the syndicate that
controls it and work my way to the top.

14
00:00:40,660 --> 00:00:44,040
Bucciarati, trust me,
I'll be a primo mafioso.

15
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:46,800
I'm open, pass it!

16
00:00:56,520 --> 00:00:57,380
Crazy mille!

17
00:00:59,060 --> 00:00:59,890
Fine then.

18
00:00:59,973 --> 00:01:02,960
I'll report I was unable
to locate Luka's attacker.

19
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:06,414
Then I'll introduce you to
begin the initiation process.

20
00:01:06,520 --> 00:01:07,696
But you should know,

21
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:11,784
if it ever gets out that you're
attempting to take down the boss,

22
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:14,118
I'll be forced to cut ties with you.

23
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:17,122
A traitor stands alone on
an island of isolation.

24
00:01:17,740 --> 00:01:20,380
Your failure will be
yours and yours alone.

25
00:01:24,040 --> 00:01:28,000
Nothing certain yet, but
your resolve is undeniable.

26
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:32,460
I respect that kind of nobility, and
I commend your golden aspirations.

27
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:34,140
You have my support.

28
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:03,500
Thank you.

29
00:02:50,380 --> 00:02:54,980
We will continue to fight We
will fight with our enemies

30
00:03:00,380 --> 00:03:02,400
Fighting gold!

31
00:03:20,380 --> 00:03:22,477
And it's not the boss's actual name.

32
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:27,325
To be frank, no one knows his true name,
nor does anyone know what he looks like.

33
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:30,504
Orders are passed down
via a multitude of kapos.

34
00:03:31,160 --> 00:03:35,925
Giorno, the kapo who will decide your
future in the familia is a man named Polpo.

35
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:37,717
Go on now.

36
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:39,800
He resides here in this building.

37
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:42,380
But this is...

38
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:44,720
It's a prison.

39
00:03:45,440 --> 00:03:46,280
That's right.

40
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:50,297
Polpo was convicted and promptly
sentenced to 15 years in prison.

41
00:03:50,380 --> 00:03:53,620
He still issues orders
and manages the Familia,

42
00:03:53,760 --> 00:03:56,017
but he does it all from
within those walls.

43
00:03:56,100 --> 00:04:00,677
He can leave his confinement whenever the
desire strikes him, but he chooses not to.

44
00:04:00,760 --> 00:04:02,580
He simply has no need.

45
00:04:03,260 --> 00:04:04,090
¿Por qué?

46
00:04:04,180 --> 00:04:05,560
Your answer's inside.

47
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,060
Listen, Giorno.

48
00:04:07,260 --> 00:04:09,897
In a matter of minutes,
he'll conduct your interview.

49
00:04:09,980 --> 00:04:11,500
It's imperative you pass.

50
00:04:11,680 --> 00:04:14,137
It's no different from
an ordinary interview.

51
00:04:14,220 --> 00:04:16,480
His mood will dictate its content.

52
00:04:17,020 --> 00:04:20,180
And remember, he cannot find out.

53
00:04:20,900 --> 00:04:21,920
I understand.

54
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:27,824
Before I forget, you mentioned
our powers are called stands, yes?

55
00:04:27,940 --> 00:04:30,700
I never asked, how did you acquire yours?

56
00:04:32,380 --> 00:04:33,860
And do others have them?

57
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:36,553
Once again, the answer's waiting inside.

58
00:04:36,820 --> 00:04:38,080
If you pass.

59
00:04:42,380 --> 00:04:43,580
Before you head in,

60
00:04:43,760 --> 00:04:47,277
I'm going to need your watch and
everything in your pockets on this tray.

61
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:49,948
After that, you can
move on to the pat-down.

62
00:05:06,140 --> 00:05:08,905
Please stand over there,
hands above your head.

63
00:05:10,560 --> 00:05:14,237
Once we open the gate, proceed forward,
then stop at the end of the hall.

64
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:15,150
Got it?

65
00:05:16,060 --> 00:05:17,766
Polpo's cell is labeled N-28.

66
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:19,259
You can't miss it.

67
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:23,957
Reinforced glass keeps him inside,
but you can still converse.

68
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:28,877
Keep in mind, exchanging objects either
from him or yourself is strictly forbidden,

69
00:05:28,960 --> 00:05:30,157
so don't try anything.

70
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:33,064
You only have 15 minutes
to complete your visit.

71
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:37,565
Once you enter, I'll
close the gate behind you.

72
00:05:37,820 --> 00:05:40,517
If he gets hostile, just
yell and we'll assist you.

73
00:05:40,600 --> 00:05:43,177
I'm talking to him while
he's locked up in his cell?

74
00:05:43,260 --> 00:05:44,997
We're not going to get a special room?

75
00:05:45,080 --> 00:05:45,910
Not a chance.

76
00:05:46,220 --> 00:05:48,020
Don't you realize who he is?

77
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:18,860
It's injured, isn't it?

78
00:06:19,500 --> 00:06:20,840
Your left arm.

79
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:29,150
What?

80
00:06:29,233 --> 00:06:30,651
I thought that was a bed.

81
00:06:33,220 --> 00:06:36,597
I spy a faint yet distinct
red marking on the fingers of

82
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:39,897
your right hand that signifies
you were gripping something.

83
00:06:39,980 --> 00:06:42,817
I'd say they're the markings
left behind by a bag.

84
00:06:42,900 --> 00:06:47,537
And based on that fact, you've been carrying
the bag exclusively in your right hand.

85
00:06:47,620 --> 00:06:49,640
Now why would that be?

86
00:06:49,900 --> 00:06:52,240
Well, first of all, you're correct.

87
00:06:52,720 --> 00:06:54,900
I carried my bag with my right hand.

88
00:06:55,200 --> 00:06:57,960
Also, I did injure my left arm earlier.

89
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:05,340
I envy your youthful
body and reckless spirit.

90
00:07:07,640 --> 00:07:09,580
By the by, do you drink wine?

91
00:07:10,040 --> 00:07:12,840
This Chianti Classico is molto buono.

92
00:07:13,140 --> 00:07:15,077
And when paired with a few crackers,

93
00:07:15,160 --> 00:07:18,640
scamorza and the right amount
of caviar, It's perfection.

94
00:07:19,100 --> 00:07:21,137
I'm not allowed to give you anything.

95
00:07:21,220 --> 00:07:23,808
And I can't accept
anything from you either.

96
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:27,080
That's just a silly formality.

97
00:07:27,420 --> 00:07:31,655
What people say when watched and what
they do when no one else is around

98
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:35,400
are two entirely different things.

99
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:40,652
Therein lies the beauty and ugliness
of this fickle thing we call humanity.

100
00:07:40,920 --> 00:07:45,120
I suppose the only real tragedy to
being holed up in this cell is...

101
00:07:46,420 --> 00:07:47,720
Well, Polpo,

102
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:52,334
he's living like a king, but that's
not the reason he stays put in there.

103
00:07:52,440 --> 00:07:54,793
It wouldn't matter if he left or stayed.

104
00:07:55,540 --> 00:07:59,740
And let's be honest, with that
carcass, he's probably safer in there.

105
00:08:00,400 --> 00:08:02,497
The thing I want to
know is how the hell the

106
00:08:02,580 --> 00:08:05,345
guards even managed to
fit in through the door.

107
00:08:05,560 --> 00:08:08,089
Bucciarati's already
told me all about you.

108
00:08:09,460 --> 00:08:12,337
So you desire to be a part
of our familia, do you?

109
00:08:12,420 --> 00:08:15,720
Uh, it was Giorno Giovanna, wasn't it?

110
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:20,600
Well then, if you're ready to begin,
let's say we commence with the interview.

111
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,260
What was that?

112
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:41,740
Am I hallucinating?

113
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:46,097
For a second, it looked like he
was munching away on his fingers.

114
00:08:46,180 --> 00:08:49,957
Or maybe this cazzone
polpo is simply another

115
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:52,452
one of those stand users like Bucciarati.

116
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:57,977
Either way, I have to do whatever it takes
to keep him from finding out about me.

117
00:08:58,060 --> 00:09:00,657
When you're separating
the wheat from the chaff,

118
00:09:00,740 --> 00:09:04,137
what do you think is the most
important factor for one to consider?

119
00:09:04,220 --> 00:09:05,900
Think carefully, Giovanna.

120
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:09,660
What a person can do, correct?

121
00:09:11,120 --> 00:09:13,500
Oh, then what can you do, ragazzo?

122
00:09:18,120 --> 00:09:21,840
While that guard was patting
me down, I took some souvenirs.

123
00:09:22,380 --> 00:09:25,380
I thought they might come
in handy during our test.

124
00:09:25,500 --> 00:09:27,971
Of course, I'll return them on my way out.

125
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:34,075
Is that all you brought to impress me?

126
00:09:34,200 --> 00:09:37,277
Well, besides that, I have this
other little trick I can do.

127
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:40,140
I can fold my ear into my ear canal.

128
00:09:43,760 --> 00:09:45,820
Ah, molto interessante.

129
00:09:47,480 --> 00:09:52,720
But you see, there's something very
important we haven't discussed yet.

130
00:09:53,400 --> 00:09:57,180
And that is the delicate subject
of trust, Giorno Giovanna.

131
00:09:57,780 --> 00:10:01,309
That's the most important quality
in selecting an associate.

132
00:10:01,460 --> 00:10:02,757
They must be trustworthy.

133
00:10:02,840 --> 00:10:05,800
When compared to that
essential characteristic,

134
00:10:06,080 --> 00:10:08,617
intelligence and talent are
no more significant than

135
00:10:08,700 --> 00:10:11,876
this piece of slobbery cracker
stuck between my teeth.

136
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:17,040
My test will tell me exactly
how trustworthy you are.

137
00:10:17,460 --> 00:10:20,342
The discerning flame of
this lighter reveals all.

138
00:10:22,540 --> 00:10:24,460
Now take it in hand and go.

139
00:10:24,900 --> 00:10:27,020
You are not to let the flame expire.

140
00:10:31,640 --> 00:10:34,740
Aspetta, I warn you,
exercise extreme caution.

141
00:10:35,120 --> 00:10:38,480
The 17th century theologian
Fuller once said,

142
00:10:38,740 --> 00:10:42,000
He's my friend that speaks
well of me behind my back.

143
00:10:42,160 --> 00:10:44,395
You'd do well to remember those words.

144
00:10:44,480 --> 00:10:46,951
If you want to become part of our familia,

145
00:10:47,260 --> 00:10:51,497
you'll need to demonstrate your
trustworthiness even when no one's looking.

146
00:10:51,580 --> 00:10:52,840
24 hours.

147
00:10:53,200 --> 00:10:55,377
That's how long you'll
possess the lighter.

148
00:10:55,460 --> 00:10:57,880
You must never let the flame go out.

149
00:10:58,980 --> 00:11:03,000
If you pass this test,
you'll be welcome to join us.

150
00:11:03,380 --> 00:11:04,497
Straightforward, yes?

151
00:11:04,580 --> 00:11:07,345
And don't worry, there's
plenty of flu in here.

152
00:11:07,780 --> 00:11:12,015
All that's required to pass is for
you to sit in your room until 3 p .m.

153
00:11:12,200 --> 00:11:14,200
tomorrow looking after that flame.

154
00:11:14,300 --> 00:11:17,597
As long as you're truly a man
of prudence and perseverance,

155
00:11:17,680 --> 00:11:19,697
then nothing should happen to that light.

156
00:11:19,780 --> 00:11:23,477
Do this simple task and you will
have proven your trustworthiness.

157
00:11:23,560 --> 00:11:25,580
But don't get too complacent.

158
00:11:25,720 --> 00:11:29,697
If you happen to be the kind of person
who would take what I have to say lightly,

159
00:11:29,780 --> 00:11:33,420
let's say you nod off, or you
sneeze, or maybe you stumble,

160
00:11:33,780 --> 00:11:37,251
or perhaps a gust of wind
extinguishes that precious flame.

161
00:11:39,040 --> 00:11:41,746
I'll know beyond a shadow
of a doubt that you,

162
00:11:41,840 --> 00:11:45,134
my friend, cannot be trusted
as a member of our familia.

163
00:11:45,560 --> 00:11:48,442
Now take the lighter and
be on your way, Cucholo.

164
00:11:49,740 --> 00:11:51,740
Behold the key to our familia.

165
00:11:59,060 --> 00:12:01,320
You have 24 hours.

166
00:12:01,800 --> 00:12:04,720
I look forward to our
second meeting tomorrow.

167
00:12:05,140 --> 00:12:06,260
3 p .m.

168
00:12:06,660 --> 00:12:07,860
Don't be late.

169
00:12:08,960 --> 00:12:10,360
24 hours.

170
00:12:10,820 --> 00:12:14,585
All visitors must proceed through
the gate for a final pat-down.

171
00:12:18,740 --> 00:12:21,177
once we give you permission
to exit the premises

172
00:12:21,260 --> 00:12:23,797
you may proceed to the
next room to retrieve

173
00:12:23,880 --> 00:12:27,017
your belongings wait a second didn't Polpo

174
00:12:27,100 --> 00:12:32,997
say anything to you time
for your search you've

175
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:35,137
been warned accepting
anything from a convict

176
00:12:35,220 --> 00:12:39,137
is punishable by law
Merida I was banking on the

177
00:12:39,220 --> 00:12:40,757
fact that he would have
bribed these cops to let

178
00:12:40,840 --> 00:12:43,437
me walk out of here with
the lighter scot-free

179
00:12:43,520 --> 00:12:44,350
Atencione!

180
00:12:44,433 --> 00:12:46,889
Hands above your head
and step forward now!

181
00:12:47,700 --> 00:12:48,530
I get it.

182
00:12:48,613 --> 00:12:50,281
Polpo's test has already started.

183
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:53,240
Which means there's no turning back.

184
00:12:53,560 --> 00:12:54,600
I have to pass.

185
00:12:54,860 --> 00:12:58,740
I have to become a part of the
Passione Familia at any cost.

186
00:13:05,240 --> 00:13:07,360
Step forward, nice and slow.

187
00:13:07,620 --> 00:13:09,977
I concealed her ID in the palm of my hand.

188
00:13:10,060 --> 00:13:11,477
I can hide this flame too.

189
00:13:11,560 --> 00:13:13,080
Here we go.

190
00:13:44,160 --> 00:13:45,260
You're good to go.

191
00:13:45,700 --> 00:13:47,937
Doesn't seem to be anything out of order.

192
00:13:48,020 --> 00:13:49,957
You're free to leave the premises.

193
00:13:50,040 --> 00:13:53,280
But first, I ask that
you show me your palms.

194
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:55,720
I'll say it once more.

195
00:13:56,160 --> 00:13:59,617
You're prohibited from accepting
any objects from convicts.

196
00:13:59,700 --> 00:14:01,582
Now open your hands immediately.

197
00:14:01,860 --> 00:14:02,801
That's an order!

198
00:14:15,900 --> 00:14:16,760
A flower?

199
00:14:19,280 --> 00:14:20,397
Well, what do you know?

200
00:14:20,480 --> 00:14:22,304
This thing is an actual flower.

201
00:14:22,960 --> 00:14:23,790
Fine.

202
00:14:23,873 --> 00:14:26,757
If this is the worst you've
got, you can have it back.

203
00:14:26,840 --> 00:14:28,400
Our visitor is free to go.

204
00:14:36,980 --> 00:14:40,877
I transformed the lighter into a flower
and hid the flame within the petals.

205
00:14:40,960 --> 00:14:43,195
Still, that was too close for comfort.

206
00:14:43,860 --> 00:14:48,448
Now that I think about it, could this
flame actually be part of Polpo's stand?

207
00:15:00,040 --> 00:15:01,677
This wind is a major problem.

208
00:15:01,760 --> 00:15:03,940
Yo, Giorno! Perfect timing!

209
00:15:04,360 --> 00:15:06,877
Hey, could you be a pal and
press the shutter button?

210
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:08,078
Nope, not a chance.

211
00:15:09,420 --> 00:15:13,477
Excuse me, youngster, but would you
mind lending me a hand with all this?

212
00:15:13,560 --> 00:15:14,390
Not now.

213
00:15:23,380 --> 00:15:25,321
Finally made it back to the dorm.

214
00:15:32,940 --> 00:15:34,220
That was a close one.

215
00:15:37,560 --> 00:15:38,390
Ow.

216
00:15:43,940 --> 00:15:45,397
This should keep it upright.

217
00:15:45,480 --> 00:15:49,377
And even if there's a little draft, it
shouldn't be enough to blow out the light.

218
00:15:49,460 --> 00:15:50,800
Now, as Polpo said,

219
00:15:51,260 --> 00:15:53,337
all I have to do is
remain diligent and watch

220
00:15:53,420 --> 00:15:56,340
this flame with my life for 23 more hours.

221
00:15:56,860 --> 00:15:58,720
Oh, that's right. The window.

222
00:15:58,980 --> 00:16:01,392
I have to make sure it's good and locked.

223
00:16:01,760 --> 00:16:05,525
You never really know when a gust
of wind might suddenly strike.

224
00:16:09,800 --> 00:16:10,630
The hell?

225
00:16:10,713 --> 00:16:12,699
Who would just go and open my door?

226
00:16:16,480 --> 00:16:17,520
Wait, that's...

227
00:16:19,140 --> 00:16:21,316
Hmm, I guess he hasn't come home yet.

228
00:16:22,560 --> 00:16:23,637
It's now or never.

229
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:25,437
Isn't that the Japanese tourist?

230
00:16:25,520 --> 00:16:27,720
Yeah, it's Koichi Hirose.

231
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:31,165
How the hell did the guy
find out where I live?

232
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:33,150
Hmm.

233
00:16:33,233 --> 00:16:36,477
He must have already done something
with my suitcase and everything inside.

234
00:16:36,560 --> 00:16:40,160
Although, he may have left my
passport around here somewhere.

235
00:16:40,660 --> 00:16:42,400
Selling off a personal ID?

236
00:16:42,780 --> 00:16:45,297
That process has got to
be a lot more involved.

237
00:16:45,380 --> 00:16:47,737
I can't believe I'm
sneaking around his room.

238
00:16:47,820 --> 00:16:49,408
I feel like a common thief.

239
00:16:49,880 --> 00:16:51,057
Oh, what am I saying?

240
00:16:51,140 --> 00:16:52,017
He's the thief!

241
00:16:52,100 --> 00:16:55,159
All I'm doing is looking
for what's rightfully mine.

242
00:16:55,780 --> 00:16:56,610
That's right!

243
00:16:56,693 --> 00:16:58,120
His passport! Katsu!

244
00:16:58,440 --> 00:17:00,028
It's in the box on my desk.

245
00:17:00,120 --> 00:17:01,677
I was gonna give it back to him.

246
00:17:01,760 --> 00:17:05,172
It's only a matter of time
before Koichi finds that flame.

247
00:17:05,600 --> 00:17:08,257
There's no question he'll
put it out once he does.

248
00:17:08,340 --> 00:17:10,458
He'll just think it's a fire hazard.

